---
description: Test-first and definition-of-done rules for emulator changes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Testing contract

- Add or extend a failing test before implementing or correcting behavior.
- Instruction changes must cover result, flags, exceptions, widths, memory forms, and relevant CPU modes.
- JIT changes require interpreter↔JIT lockstep/differential tests.
- Snapshot/format changes require round-trip and version-compat tests.
- Device register changes require device-level tests (reset, R/W, interrupts when applicable).

# Done means green gates

Before claiming complete, run what exists for the workspace:

```bash
cargo fmt --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo test --workspace
```

Also run Wasm build, browser tests, and oracle diffs when those targets exist.

# Report format

- Files changed
- Spec sections used
- Tests added
- Commands run and results
- Unsupported cases remaining
